  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A researcher who makes",
    "overview": "The portfolio keeps the user-approved Apple-like monochrome interface, generous spacing, and rounded image frames. The user-selected Hanken Grotesk gives headings a clear, personal voice; Onest supports the longer research reading. Original project artifacts and personal photographs keep their own colors. The Home portrait is a generated painted-style transformation of the supplied source portrait.\n\nHome introduces Nishabh and his making practice. Home and Work show all four documented research projects together; Work adds contribution, role, and method details for comparison and inspection. Both use open layouts, hairline separators, and direct actions. The crochet activity invites reversible making on both Home and Work, alongside the actual work-in-progress photographs on Home and About.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
